From 813b4f7b82fb7a4a1d7e92ee8bd2222080400183 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:45:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] Add Receipt Templates, Barcode/QR Search, Reports
 filters, Full-screen, Dark/Light mode, and cart totals

1. Receipt Templates
   - Wire the existing Classic/Modern + 58mm/80mm Settings UI up to
     SettingController (was previously display-only in settings.js).
   - New assets/js/receipt-template.js: single shared renderer + Code 39
     barcode builder used by both the live POS receipt and a new
     'Preview receipt' modal on the Settings page (sample data, no
     server round trip).
   - CSS: .pos-receipt-tpl-classic/modern and .pos-receipt-w58/w80
     variants, plus width-aware @page print sizing so printed receipts
     match the configured paper width instead of a generic A4 sheet.
   - Seed + migration for the receipt_template/printer_width Settings
     keys so existing installs get sane defaults.

2. Barcode / QR Code Search
   - New scanner modal on the POS Screen (Camera tab via html5-qrcode,
     Manual input tab with a Search-by: Barcode/Product number/Product
     name selector).
   - Sale::searchProducts() and PosController::products() gained an
     optional search_by filter so the manual tab can search a single
     field precisely; the existing combined search is unchanged.
   - Both the camera and manual paths reuse pos.js's existing
     lookup/add-to-cart pipeline (exposed as window.POSCart) instead of
     duplicating it.

3. Business Reports
   - Added Yesterday and This Year date-range presets alongside the
     existing Today/Week/Month.
   - Added a Returns/Refunds KPI (voided-sale count + amount) via a new
     Report::returnsSummary() query, exposed through ReportController.

4. Full-Screen
   - Navbar toggle button using the Fullscreen API, with an icon that
     tracks fullscreenchange (works alongside the existing mobile
     auto-fullscreen setting).

5. Dark / Light Mode
   - Navbar toggle button; Light is the default.
   - Preference is saved to localStorage and applied by an inline
     script in includes/header.php before the stylesheet paints, so
     there's no flash of the wrong theme.
   - Dark variant re-points the existing --pos-* CSS custom properties,
     covering navbar/sidebar/cards/tables/inputs/modals in one pass.
     Printed receipts intentionally stay light (they mirror paper).

6. Total Quantity / Items
   - POS Screen cart summary now shows 'Items: N' and 'Total Qty: N'
     above the subtotal/tax/total, updating live as the cart changes.
