From a2de607e50db7d44331e0b62d10e61a972e99ef5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 07:06:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/22] Add End of Day button+modal on POS Screen, and per-item
 bargained price/discount in the cart

End of Day (POS Screen)
- New 'End of Day' button in the POS header, next to Held. Opens a
  modal containing the exact same Transaction Record + cash
  reconciliation UI as the standalone Reconciliation page - reuses
  assets/js/reconciliation.js as-is (same element IDs, just embedded
  in a modal) rather than duplicating the logic.
- reconciliation.js now defers its first load until the modal is
  actually opened (shown.bs.modal) when embedded this way, instead of
  firing a request on every POS page load; the standalone page is
  unaffected and still loads immediately.

Per-item price edit (bargain/negotiate) + per-item discount
- Sale::priceCart() already supported a client-supplied unit_price
  (capped at the catalog price - never above it) and a per-line
  discount, but pos.js never exposed either in the UI, and buildPayload()
  stripped both back out before sending to checkout. Both are now wired
  up end-to-end:
  - Each cart row has two small inline fields under the item name: a
    price box (capped client-side at catalog price, mirroring the
    server-side cap) and a discount box (capped at the line's own
    subtotal). A 'Bargained' badge appears when the price has been
    negotiated below catalog.
  - computeTotals() and renderCart()'s line-total math now include the
    per-item discount alongside the product's automatic discount_rate.
  - buildPayload() now sends unit_price/discount per item instead of
