From 04aff166b8b158b849075e7739cebeac45e38c9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 02:19:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/22] Fix per-line cart total (was double-adding tax), align
 End of Day button, and add Senior Citizen / PWD discount

Cart line-total bug
- The cart's per-line Total column was including tax on top of
  price x quantity (e.g. a catalog price of 80 with an 11% product tax
  rate displayed as 88.80). Total now shows price x quantity minus that
  line's own discounts only; tax stays aggregated in the Subtotal/Tax/
  Discount/Total summary below, where it already belonged.

End of Day button alignment
- It was using the large .pos-v2-complete style (48px min-height) next
  to small btn-sm date-nav buttons, so it stood out at the wrong
  height. Now uses a proper .pos-btn-eod class built on Bootstrap's
  btn-sm base, matching its neighbors' height exactly while keeping a
  distinct accent color.

Senior Citizen / PWD discount
- New Settings section: enable/disable toggle + configurable discount
  rate (default 20%, matching PH statutory rate) - never trusted from
  the client, always read server-side at checkout.
- New Sales.senior_pwd_type / senior_pwd_id_number / senior_pwd_discount
  columns (migration + updated seed) recording which discount was
  applied, the required ID number, and the peso amount, for the
  receipt and future reporting.
- Sale::priceCart()/checkout() compute the discount on the subtotal net
  of item/manual/loyalty discounts, before tax, and require an ID
  number whenever a type is selected.
- POS Payment modal: checkbox to apply the discount, Senior Citizen/PWD
  radio choice, ID number field, and a live preview line. pos.js's
  computeTotals() mirrors the backend's exact two-pass math (loyalty
  redemption cap uses the pre-loyalty senior/PWD base, matching the
  server) so the on-screen total matches what checkout will actually
  charge. Deliberately not persisted to the browser draft, since it
  carries a customer ID number - always starts unchecked on a new sale.
- Receipt now itemizes the Senior/PWD discount with its ID number when
  applied.
