From fe697e6929eae966ccfb1c93cebd7c5b4363b74c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 07:48:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/22] Harden checkout against client/server total drift,
 replace manual-discount textbox with an Additional Discount widget, and fix
 receipt-after-sale gating
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Checkout robustness (all payment/discount/loyalty/senior-PWD combinations)
- buildPayload() no longer calls computeTotals() a second, independent
  time - doCheckout() now computes totals ONCE and passes that exact
  object into both the paid-vs-total guard check and the actual
  checkout payload, so the two can never disagree about what's owed.
- Added a re-entrancy guard (isCheckingOut) so a fast double-click/tap
  can't submit the same sale twice.
- The paid-vs-total comparison now happens in whole centavos rather
  than raw floats, removing any sub-centavo floating-point edge case.
- Verified consistent behavior across: cash only; cash + additional
  discount; + Senior/PWD; + loyalty redemption; split payments across
  Cash/Card/GCash/Maya/Check; and every combination of the above -
  Payment Complete now shows (with a correct, non-negative change) in
  each case.

Additional Discount widget (replaces the old manual-discount textbox)
- Removed the plain number input from the cart summary's Discount row
  - it's now a plain computed label, matching every other summary row.
- Added a proper 'Additional discount' widget to the Payment modal,
  below the Subtotal/Tax/Discount/Total block: 5/10/20/25% presets, a
  Value field, and a %/₱ mode toggle - computed on the subtotal net of
  item-level discounts, before tax, same base the Senior/PWD discount
  already uses so the two stack predictably. The computed peso amount
  is what's sent to checkout, so the backend needed no changes.
- Wired into saveDraft/loadDraft/resetCart in place of the old single
  manualDiscount value.
- Removed now-dead CSS that targeted the old textbox's wrapper markup.

Receipt-after-sale setting fix
- 'Show receipt after sale' is now a true master switch: 'Auto print
  receipts' can no longer force the receipt to appear when 'Show
  receipt after sale' is unchecked (previously an independent OR
  condition let auto-print override it). Settings page now also
  disables (and unchecks) 'Auto print' whenever 'Show receipt after
  sale' is off, so the dependency is visible, not just enforced
  silently.
