From a20805b4dbbad0b0aba55b69552f0534fb4a39ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 06:03:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/22] Fix single-digit input bug in Senior/PWD and Additional
 Discount fields; verify checkout guard with targeted boundary fuzz testing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause of 'only one digit' bug
- updateAdditionalDiscountAppliedView()/updateSeniorPwdAppliedView()
  were wired into updatePaymentModalTotals(), which runs on every
  keystroke in the ID number / discount value fields. The instant the
  field held a non-empty/non-zero value, these functions collapsed
  the form (d-none) to show the 'applied' summary - hiding the very
  input the person was mid-keystroke in, so only the first digit ever
  registered before the field vanished from under the cursor.
- Fix: these two functions are no longer called from the per-keystroke
  totals refresh. Added explicit 'Apply' buttons to both widgets - the
  form now stays open and editable (with totals still updating live
  underneath, since that recompute is unaffected) until Apply is
  clicked, which is the only thing that now triggers the collapse to
  the compact summary view. Remove reverses it, as before. Senior/PWD's
  Apply also validates the ID number is present before collapsing.
- resetCart() now explicitly re-syncs both widgets to their
  (collapsed-if-empty) reset state instead of relying on incidental
  side effects.

Checkout guard verification (per request: process + scenarios tested)
- Extended the client/server fuzz harness from the previous session to
  simulate the ACTUAL 'Save Sale' guard, not just totals equality:
  800 randomized carts, each with a random mix of item-level discounts,
  tax-inclusive on/off, Additional Discount (peso or percent), Senior/
  PWD discount, loyalty redemption, and a 1-3 way split payment summed
  to the total at three boundary cases (exact, +1 centavo, -1 centavo)
  - comparing the client-side guard's pass/fail decision against the
    real PHP pricing logic's pass/fail decision. 0 mismatches.
- Also ran one fully concrete worked example exercising every feature
  at once (item discount + ₱200 additional discount + 20% Senior/PWD +
  10 loyalty points redeemed + a 2-way Cash/GCash split payment) end to
  end through both the client math and the actual PHP pricing code -
  totals matched exactly and the split payment correctly covered the
  total with the guard passing.
