From 0b1db7c8d2f7f6494c4abf0cb71bdfcbd625b815 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:26:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] Fix the actual root cause of false 'combined payments
 are less than the total due' rejections: a variable name collision in
 Sale::priceCart()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause (found by directly re-reading the live priceCart() code
against two real screenshots showing an exact-matching payment still
rejected):

Inside priceCart()'s per-item loop, the per-item manual discount was
computed into a local variable named $manualDiscount - the EXACT same
name as the function's own parameter representing the cart-level
Additional Discount (plus, during checkout(), the loyalty discount
folded into it). PHP does not scope loop-local variables separately
from the enclosing function, so every iteration silently overwrote the
parameter with that item's own per-item discount amount. By the time
the loop ended, $manualDiscount held whichever item's per-item discount
happened to run last - NOT the real Additional Discount the cashier
entered - and every downstream calculation (Senior/PWD base, discount
total, grand total) used that corrupted value instead.

For a single-item cart where the per-item and additional discounts
happened to be equal, this was invisible (the wrong value coincidentally
matched the right one). For any multi-item cart, or any cart where they
differed, the server would silently drop most or all of the intended
additional discount and demand a much higher total than the client
displayed - exactly the reported symptom of an exact/sufficient payment
still being rejected.

Fix: renamed the loop-local variable to $itemManualDiscount. The
function parameter is now never touched inside the loop.

Verified with a standalone before/after reproduction
(/tmp/totals_check/verify_fix.php, not part of the deliverable) using
the same shape of cart shown in the bug report screenshot (3 items with
small, different per-item discounts + a ₱1000 additional discount):
the buggy version computed a grand_total of ₱1087.22 (silently
dropping the ₱1000 discount down to ₱0.50), while the fixed version
correctly computes ₱87.72 - matching what the client displays and what
a cashier would actually pay.
---
 app/models/Sale.php | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/models/Sale.php b/app/models/Sale.php
index af5f1f8..0312191 100644
--- a/app/models/Sale.php
+++ b/app/models/Sale.php
@@ -218,9 +218,18 @@ class Sale
             // Per-item manual discount (on top of the product's own
             // automatic discount_rate, if any) - clamped so a line can
             // never go negative regardless of what the client sends.
+            // NOTE: this MUST NOT be named $manualDiscount - that name is
+            // the function's cart-level "additional discount" parameter,
+            // and reusing it here silently overwrote it on every loop
+            // iteration (to whichever item's per-item discount happened
+            // to run last), corrupting the Senior/PWD base and the final
+            // total for any multi-item cart, or any cart where the last
+            // item's per-item discount differed from the additional
+            // discount actually entered - exactly the "combined payments
+            // are less than the total due" false rejections being seen.
             $requestedDiscount = max(0.0, (float) ($item['discount'] ?? 0));
-            $manualDiscount = min($requestedDiscount, max(0.0, $grossExclusive - $productDiscount));
-            $lineDiscount = round($productDiscount + $manualDiscount, 2);
+            $itemManualDiscount = min($requestedDiscount, max(0.0, $grossExclusive - $productDiscount));
+            $lineDiscount = round($productDiscount + $itemManualDiscount, 2);
 
             // Tax is computed on the tax-exclusive amount AFTER item-level
             // discounts, not on the full pre-discount price - a discounted
