From 75c63fec57850f7a6c2a89367c5fc9b9eef03243 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:25:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/22] Fix sidebar scroll (Settings unreachable on mobile/100%
 zoom); add Start Shift / End Shift feature

Sidebar scroll fix
- .pos-sidebar previously grew to fit its content with no independent
  scroll region, so on a short/100%-zoomed browser window - or on
  mobile, where it's a fixed slide-out panel - the last nav item
  (Settings) could end up below the visible area with no way to reach
  it.
- Desktop: sidebar is now position: sticky, pinned to the viewport
  height (calc(100vh - 64px) below the navbar) with its own
  overflow-y: auto, independent of the main content column's height.
- Mobile: the existing fixed slide-out panel now also gets its own
  overflow-y: auto (plus -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch), anchored
  by top/bottom instead of a content-driven height.

Start Shift / End Shift (per-cashier register sessions)
- New dbo.Shifts table (shift_number, business_date, user_id, opening/
  actual/expected cash, variance, notes, status, timestamps) and a new
  Sales.shift_id column, so each sale is stamped with which shift it
  was rung up under - shift totals are exact, not approximated from a
  user+time-window guess. New migration_shifts.sql for existing
  installs; pos_store.sql updated for fresh ones.
- Shift model: getActive/getById, live summary() (Net Sales, Items
  Sold, Cash Sales, Transactions - cash figures read from SalePayments,
  matching the same approach as Reconciliation), lastClosedCash() to
  suggest the next shift's opening float, start()/end() with variance
  calculation.
- ShiftController (any logged-in POS user manages their own shift, no
  extra role restriction - every cashier needs one to use the register)
  + assets/js/pos-shift.js, wired into the POS Screen:
  - Start Shift modal: Opening Cash, a Quick Count denomination
    breakdown that auto-fills Opening Cash, a banner suggesting the
    previous shift's counted cash, notes. Shown automatically when a
    cashier has no active shift; Cancel lets them proceed without one
    (shifts are optional, not enforced).
  - A live shift badge + dropdown panel in the POS header (cashier,
    duration, Total Sales, Cash Sales, Transactions, End Shift),
    polling every 30s plus an immediate nudge right after each sale.
  - End Shift modal: Net Sales, Items Sold, a cash reconciliation
    breakdown (Opening + Cash Sales = Expected), an Actual Cash count
    defaulting to Expected, notes, variance computed on submit.
- Sale::checkout() now stamps new sales with the cashier's active
  shift_id (null if they have none), reading it via Shift::getActive().
