From 5fcf2a5c88f272afac24b3cd63892b3d2b8d2fe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 06:27:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/22] Fix tax-vs-discount regression, harden checkout against
 unmigrated databases, move Shift feature into the global nav, polish End
 Shift button
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tax/discount/subtotal regression fix
- An earlier session's tax-inclusive fix accidentally changed tax to
  be computed on the POST-discount amount everywhere, not just in
  tax-inclusive mode. This app has always taxed the sticker price
  itself (Tax = price x rate, independent of any discount) - confirmed
  by checking the original pre-existing priceCart() from before any of
  this work began. Restored that: tax is computed on the full
  tax-exclusive line amount, unaffected by item-level discounts, in
  BOTH client (pos.js) and server (Sale::priceCart()). Tax-inclusive
  extraction (backing tax out of an inclusive sticker price) is
  unaffected - that part was a genuine new feature, not a regression.
  Verified against the exact numbers from the bug report (₱1000 item,
  12% tax, 10% discount): now correctly computes Tax=₱120, Total=₱1020
  instead of the regressed Tax=₱108, Total=₱1008.

Checkout hardened against partially-migrated databases
- Sale::checkout() was unconditionally querying the Shifts table and
  referencing Sales.shift_id/senior_pwd_* columns added by this
  session's migrations. On a database that hasn't run
  migration_shifts.sql and/or migration_pwd_senior_discount.sql yet,
  this broke EVERY checkout with a generic 'Checkout failed.' (a raw
  SQL error surfacing through the generic failure handler) - not just
  those specific features being unavailable.
- Added a cached per-column existence check; the INSERT's column/value
  lists and parameter bindings for shift_id, senior_pwd_type,
  senior_pwd_id_number, and senior_pwd_discount are now only included
  when those columns actually exist. Checkout works identically to
  before those migrations existed on a database that hasn't run them,
  and the shift lookup itself is also wrapped so a lookup problem can
  never block a sale from completing.

Shift feature moved into the persistent nav (was previously scoped to
the POS Screen's own header only - completing work left unfinished
from an earlier session)
- Start Shift / End Shift modals now live in includes/shift-modals.php,
  included once site-wide via includes/footer.php, and the shift badge
  lives in includes/navbar.php - so the active-shift indicator is
  visible from any page, styled consistently with the existing
  notification-bell dropdown pattern (same panel/row structure, theme
  colors).
- The auto-prompt to start a shift still only fires on the POS Screen
  itself (checks for #posV2) - checking Reports or Settings with no
  active shift doesn't interrupt the cashier; the badge simply stays
  hidden there until a shift exists.
- Restyled the 'End Shift' trigger inside the nav panel from a muted
  outline button to the same solid dark-fill treatment used for other
  'close/confirm' actions in the app (Complete Sale, Save
  Reconciliation), instead of looking like a disabled/secondary action.
- Confirmed the End Shift modal's confirm button is already correctly
  disabled whenever Actual Cash is 0 or empty (was already wired from
  the earlier session; verified it initializes correctly - enabled
  when the modal opens with a non-zero expected amount, and reactively
  disables if the cashier clears the field).
