Subject: [PATCH 16/22] Fix zero padding on the Shift Active panel and widen
 its mobile-responsive breakpoint

Padding fix
- The panel's div had Bootstrap's 'p-0' utility class alongside our
  own .pos-shift-panel padding rule. Bootstrap utilities apply
  padding: 0 !important, which always wins over a non-important rule
  regardless of specificity or source order - so our intended
  16px/18px padding was being silently zeroed out, and every row's
  text sat flush against the panel's edges exactly as reported.
  Removed p-0 from the markup (the notification panel's own p-0 is
  left alone - that one's a deliberate flush-list design where each
  item supplies its own padding, a different pattern). Also removed
  the shift panel foot's now-redundant horizontal padding, which had
  been compensating for the p-0 by adding its own 16px - with the
  parent's padding restored, that doubled the foot's inset compared to
  the header/body above it.

Mobile responsiveness
- Widened the breakpoint that switches the panel to a fixed,
  viewport-anchored, full-width layout from max-width: 575.98px (only
  the narrowest phones) to 767.98px, covering more phones and narrow/
  tablet-width windows where the dropdown could otherwise still
  overflow past the edge of the screen.
