From 9c4f19ad46d4a4df6c16d7bbeecc8f6f6c40eaad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 05:53:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] Require an active shift before Complete Sale opens the
 Payment modal

Previously, cancelling the Start Shift prompt let a cashier use the
POS indefinitely with no shift at all - every subsequent sale would
just carry shift_id = NULL, silently invisible to Shift/Reconciliation
reporting.

- New window.POSShift.requireShift(): returns true if a shift is
  already active, otherwise re-shows the (already-populated) Start
  Shift modal and returns false.
- #btnOpenPayment now calls this before opening the Payment modal -
  clicking 'Complete sale' with no active shift shows Start Shift
  instead. Cancelling it just returns to the cart, same as always;
  clicking Complete Sale again re-prompts. Once a shift is started,
  Complete Sale proceeds straight to Payment as normal.
- Guarded with a typeof/existence check so this has zero effect if the
  Shifts migration hasn't been run (window.POSShift wouldn't exist) -
  checkout keeps working exactly as before on a database that hasn't
  adopted shifts at all, consistent with shifts being an opt-in
  feature rather than a hard requirement enforced everywhere.
- Hold Sale is intentionally left ungated - only completing an actual
  sale requires a shift, matching what was asked.
