From d812e6c33ab0eb393add99d32873204881d44bf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 21:29:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] Fix Dashboard and Reports charts: missing zero-fill
 days, split-payment misattribution, and dark mode support

Data accuracy fixes (Report.php - shared by both Dashboard and Reports)

- Report::salesByDay() previously only returned rows for days that
  actually had a sale, so both the Dashboard's 'Daily revenue' chart
  and the Reports page's 'Sales Trend' chart silently compressed or
  skipped empty days instead of showing a proper flat/zero line for
  them - a week with sales on only 2 of 7 days rendered as a 2-point
  line, not a 7-day trend. Now zero-fills every date in the requested
  range.
- Report::paymentBreakdown() grouped by Sales.payment_method, which
  stores the literal string 'multiple' for any split payment - every
  split-payment sale was dumped into one unhelpful 'MULTIPLE' bucket
  on the Dashboard's payment-methods donut chart and the Reports
  page's payment breakdown, instead of being attributed to the actual
  methods used. Now sums real per-method amounts from SalePayments,
  the same fix already applied to Reconciliation's cash breakdown
  earlier this session.

Dark mode support (charts render to <canvas>, so they never picked up
CSS variables or the [data-theme] attribute on their own)
- Both dashboard.js and reports.js now resolve axis/legend/gridline
  colors from the current theme at render time, and redraw
  immediately - not just on next page load - when the theme is
  toggled. assets/js/app.js's theme toggle now dispatches a
  'pos:theme-changed' window event for exactly this purpose.
- Unified the Sales Trend chart's color from an unrelated green to the
  same accent orange used by the Dashboard's revenue chart (and every
  other 'primary metric' accent in the app) - same underlying metric,
  was inexplicably a different color depending on which page you were
  on. Also unified date-axis label formatting (MM-DD) between the two.
---
